# Pinned 2026-10-02 by panel 187's compiler engineer, route (1f): a known
# cost, not an intent; a change in either direction turns this case red.
# Python's one-line suites: the colon habit is told once on a line
# (`parse/colon_habit.hero:98`, its fix certain), and the next head's colon
# is named a missing body (`parse/opening.hero:274`), found the `:`. Rows
# 131-56a and 131-56b. Class (a): `adjacent`.

function two_colons(n: i64)
    if n > 0: if n > 1: print(1)  #~ trailing_colon missing_body

function three_colons(n: i64)
    if n > 0: if n > 1: if n > 2: print(1)  #~ trailing_colon missing_body

function main()
    print(1)
